    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "KLIMT IS COMING . A major work by Gustav Klimt will go under the hammer at Christie’s New York next month with a price tag of $60 to $80 million, and it’s guaranteed to sell, reports ARTnews . If sold on November 17th, Klimt’s lush, green landscape painting Litzlbergkeller (1915-1916), which has been in the same private collection for nearly three decades, would put it among the Austrian artist’s top prices at public sale. The current, unnamed owner paid $14.7 million for it at Sotheby’s in 1997, which is the equivalent of $30.9 million today. “The inn of Litzlbergkeller sits at the water’s edge, between Klimt’s allover technique and abstraction, form and dissolution, prewar and certainties and the unknown,” said Max Carter , global chairman of 20th and 21st century art. Klimt’s current auction record is for Portrait of Elisabeth Lederer (1914-16), sold at Sotheby’s, New York in November 2025 for $236.4 million.",
