    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "IN MEMORIAM . Photographer Miguel Bergasa , who photographed Paraguay’s religious Mennonite community, has died, reports El País . Born in Pamplona, Spain, in 1951, Bergasa was known for his black-and-white documentary photographs of rural festivals and rituals at risk of erasure. “I like to capture images of things you know time will erase. There’s a sense of longing,” he once said.",
